# Privacy and secrets

- Samples: synthetic, or contributed with explicit consent, anonymised before they touch the repo. Placeholders: `PARTY_A`, `PHONE_1`, `SHOP_1`, `ADDR_1`.
- Never put in the repo: audio, real chats, phone numbers, CNICs, addresses, real shop or person names, screenshots of chats, API keys.
- `.env` is gitignored. `.env.example` lists variable names with a one-line comment each and no values. If a secret must exist, give the command to generate it locally; do not generate and show it.
- The library does not log, store or send message text unless the integrator configures it. Tests must prove the rules-only path makes no network calls.
- Run `scripts/privacy-scan.sh` before every commit that touches data, docs or fixtures. A hit blocks the commit until resolved.
- Data licence is undecided (D5). Do not publish, upload or release any dataset until the owner chooses one.
- Pakistani data-protection requirements are researched in spike N4 and are not legal advice. Do not state legal conclusions as fact.
- Removal: every contributed sample must be removable on request; keep the consent reference and sample id so removal is possible.
